<title>NETHERLANDS: Akzo Nobel shares jump on Remeron trial.</title>
<headline>Akzo Nobel shares jump on Remeron trial.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in chemical group Akzo Nobel NV rose 6.00 guilders or more than three percent to 199.00 on Tuesday after news late on Monday of positive trials of its antidepressant drug Remeron.</p>
<p>In a post-bourse announcement on Monday, Akzo said trials of the drug, manufactured by its Organon unit, had shown it to be more effective than the world's best-selling antidepressant Prozac made by Eli Lilly.</p>
<p>But dealers noted volume in the stock was fairly light at just below 500,000 contracts.</p>
<p>--Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
